WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.840
They say that there are no new ideas in Hollywood.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:04.620
And to that, we say: good.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.900
After all, why waste time coming up with a
bad new idea when you can just remake a classic,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.520
old, good idea?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.820
If something was a hit once, chances are it
will be a hit again, which is why Hollywood

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.600
is currently working on another slew of awesome
reboots.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.500
Here's a look at some upcoming remakes that
will get you pumped.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.440
Little Shop of Horrors

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:28.220
The original 1960 version of Little Shop of
Horrors was directed Roger Corman and featured

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.470
a brief appearance by a masochistic Jack Nicholson.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.720
"This is gonna hurt you more than it hurts
me."

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.760
"Oh goodie goodie!

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:35.860
Here it comes!"

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.600
The film inspired an off-Broadway musical,
which in turn gave birth to the 1986 movie

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.780
directed by Frank Oz.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.840
Now, it looks like Tinseltown is opening up
Little Shop for a third time.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.040
Deadline calls the new project "a fresh version
of the 30-year-old Frank Oz-directed film,"

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.700
but on this go-round, Greg Berlanti will be
the one shouting "action."

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.180
If Berlanti's name sounds familiar, that's
because he's the producer behind TV hits like

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.220
Riverdale, The Flash, and Supergirl.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.060
Hey, if anyone can defeat Audrey II, it's
the maid of might!

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.560
The Fly

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.880
If you're a horror fan, you know the original
Fly starring Vincent Price hit theaters back

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.060
in 1958.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.360
"ah."

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.200
"ah."

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:27.920
And in 1986, David Cronenberg decided to give
the tale his own grotesque spin, casting Jeff

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.340
Goldblum and Geena Davis in one of the nastiest
monster movies ever made.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.440
Now it looks like J.D. Dillard might very
well create his own insect monstrosity.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:43.320
In March 2017, Variety reported that the up-and-coming
director is in talks for The Fly, coming off

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.580
his critically acclaimed debut Sleight.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.820
Dillard told SlashFilm that if he ends up
directing the film, he'll be focusing on the

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:51.540
characters and not the effects, saying,

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:56.819
"I think if you look at a lot of remakes,
and the ones that may have not been as successful

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.080
as others, I think often times the wrong pieces
are remade."

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.980
White Men Can't Jump

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.540
In 1992, Woody Harrelson and Wesley Snipes
joined forces in the classic basketball comedy

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.580
White Men Can't Jump, written and directed
by Ron Shelton.

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:15.720
The film was a major hit, earning over $90
million worldwide, so it's no wonder Hollywood

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.600
is interested in a remake, with Black-ish
showrunner Kenya Barris producing and writing.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.300
And if there's one thing we know from watching
Black-ish, it's that he's got game.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.940
Does he think he can do better?

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.860
"Bring it on, bad boy!"

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:29.420
First Blood

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.940
We all know Rambo can survive in the woods,
fight the Viet Cong, and shoot helicopters

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.520
with explosive-tipped arrows.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.160
But can he sing and dance?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.960
Well, it looks like we're about to find out,
as the action movie icon is headed to…

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:43.820
Bollywood.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.100
Starring up-and-coming actor Tiger Shroff,
the First Blood remake will be titled Rambo,

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.760
and according to Entertainment Weekly,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.540
"[The movie will follow] the last surviving
member of an elite covert unit of the Indian

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.700
Armed Forces who returns home to find that
his land is in the midst of war."

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:04.280
Filming on Rambo has been delayed for now,
but they do have a cool poster, so here's

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.460
hoping it comes out soon!

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.280
Charlie's Angels

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.319
The classic 1970's TV series Charlie's Angels
was relaunched as a successful film series

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:13.920
in 2000.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.860
But Sony apparently figures it's been long
enough for yet another try, as a new big screen

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:21.780
version is reportedly set for a 2019 release.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.500
Nobody has actually been cast in it yet, but
Elizabeth Banks is set to direct, and Kristen

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.020
Stewart and Lupita N'yongo are rumored to
be in the running for roles.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.020
The Cannonball Run

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:38.700
Despite being critically panned, 1981's Cannonball
Run became a cult hit, spawning a sequel thanks

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.659
to a massive all-star cast that included everyone
from Burt Reynolds and Roger Moore to Sammy

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.500
Davis Jr. and Jackie Chan.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:50.379
Now it looks like the racers are revving their
engines again, as Universal is bringing The

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.400
Cannonball Run back to theaters.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:57.360
According to Deadline, Thomas Lennon and Robert
Ben Garant of Night at the Museum fame might

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.340
write the script, while Dodgeball director
Rawson Thurber is attached as well.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.440
Here's hoping they somehow tie Captain Chaos
into the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.020
"help is on the way!

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.300
Justice will triumph!

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.300
Dun Dun DUNNNNN!"

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.240
Alien Nation

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:18.940
The 1988 film Alien Nation was a big enough
hit that it spawned a spinoff TV series.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.400
So it makes sense that Fox might want to do
a remake.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:26.260
However, according to director Jeff Nichols,
his upcoming remake of Alien Nation isn't

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.250
a remake at all, telling ScreenCrush,

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.980
"It doesn't really have anything to do with
the original."

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:36.260
Turns out Nichols and Fox decided to slap
the Alien Nation label on a totally unrelated

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.240
project the director was developing, because,
why not.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:44.000
We don't know what the story is about, but
at least fans know what it's not about, so

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.380
that's something, right?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.120
Flash Gordon

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:53.600
In 2015, it was announced that Matthew Vaughn—the
guy behind Kick-Ass, X-Men: First Class, and

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.560
both Kingsmen films—would be remaking Flash
Gordon.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.540
There's just one problem, though - Guardians
of the Galaxy.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.060
Vaughn told Collider,

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.260
"The only problem with Flash Gordon is Guardians
kind of stole what I would have liked to have

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:06.760
done with it."

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.560
As a result, the upcoming Flash Gordon film
has been delayed while Vaughn tries to figure

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:12.500
out how to do it.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.380
Good luck, Matt!

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:15.840
"BONG!"

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.200
Nosferatu

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.320
Before Twilight... before Blade... there was...

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.680
Nosferatu!

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:30.400
The first full length vampire movie starred
Max Schreck as the rat-like Count Orlok, an

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:34.520
undead demon who sent audiences into hysterics
in 1922.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:39.900
Nearly a century later, the film set to be
remade by The Witch director Robert Eggers,

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:45.340
starring The Witch actress Anya Taylor-Joy
and famed creature specialist Doug Jones as

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:45.980
the vampire.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.620
Just when the film will go into production
is up in the air, but we can't wait to see

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.120
it when it finally arrives.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.180
Pet Sematary

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:58.720
According to Variety, Paramount is planning
to remake the classic Stephen King story Pet

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.480
Sematary, with Starry Eyes directors Kevin
Kolsch and Dennis Widmyer set to direct.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:08.120
No word yet on who is going to star in it,
but given the spotty track record of recent

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:13.200
King adaptations, here's hoping this one is
more like It and less like The Dark Tower.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.760
Yet another King remake?

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.800
"It's really going to happen isn't it?"

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.660
"Oh yes it is."

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.240
Logan's Run

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:25.760
It won a special Oscar for its visual effects,
but in the four decades since Logan Run's

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.260
release, the movie has largely been forgotten
by mainstream audiences.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:34.080
Directed by Michael Anderson, this sci-fi
film was set in a futuristic society where

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.900
people are executed once they reach their
30th birthday.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.640
"Well no one has to die at 30!

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.860
You can live!"

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.840
It's a sci-fi premise that's begging for a
modern take, and we'll soon get a remake courtesy

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.780
of Simon Kinberg, who wrote X-Men: Days of
Future Past and X-Men: Apocalypse.

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:56.420
No word on who will star, but according to
Deadline, they may make the lead a woman this

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.600
time around, so it should be interesting to
see what direction they head with it.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.260
Highlander

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.300
Among immortal swordsmen, there can be only
one.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:10.120
But if we're talking about movies about immortal
swordsmen, well, that's a totally different

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:10.620
story.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:16.360
There have been multiple live-action Highlander
movies, a couple of TV series, and a cartoon.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:20.780
And now it looks like Lionsgate is finally
moving forward with the long-awaited remake

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:25.280
of the 1986 cult classic, with John Wick director
Chad Stahelski attached.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.420
And hey, no matter what happens, it's guaranteed
to be better than Highlander 2!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:30.800
"Ah."

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.180
Fantastic Voyage

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.580
It's one of those science fiction classics
that's largely been forgotten by modern-day

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.080
audiences.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:47.480
Starring Raquel Welch and Donald Pleasence,
the 1966 hit Fantastic Voyage follows a group

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:52.540
of scientists who shrink down to microscopic
size, climb inside a miniature submarine,

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:56.820
and set sail inside a comatose patient, hoping
to save him from a brain clot.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.600
It's a pretty cool premise, one that's just
perfect for a remake—and fortunately for

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.140
sci-fi fans, Guillermo del Toro is the man
who'll bring this tiny story to the big screen.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:11.920
Originally, the movie was supposed to hit
theaters in 2019, but production was paused

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.960
so del Toro could focus on promoting The Shape
of Water.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.980
Things appear to be back on track now, though.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:22.740
So assuming this really is the Oscar-winner's
next project, this sci-fi adventure will definitely

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:23.540
be worth the wait.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.600
Flight of the Navigator

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:29.520
Tron wasn't the only cut sci-fi hit Disney
released in the '80s.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:34.060
They also put out Flight of the Navigator,
which was about a kid who is abducted by aliens

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:38.110
and implanted with all sorts of secret knowledge
that the government desperately wants their

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:38.620
hands on.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:43.380
Now, Lionsgate and the Henson Company are
teaming up for a new adaptation, and after

00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:48.710
briefly considering Colin Trevorrow in 2012,
they're hiring Joe Henderson—the showrunner

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.660
behind Lucifer—to pen the screenplay.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.680
And with the Henson Company's involvement,
we've got our fingers crossed that we might

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.700
get to see a few cool puppets.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:02.740
"You're very lucky slave, only the emperor
can drink you essence."

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.080
Okay... maybe not.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.820
But hopefully, we'll at least get Paul Reubens
back as the wisecracking computer.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.820
"Don't forget to feed Brutus!

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.960
Two all beef patties, special sauce, lettuce
cheese, pickles onions on a sesame seed bun

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.220
...whoa, huh huh!"

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:20.180
Cleopatra Jones

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:25.959
While not as famous as Pam Grier, Tamara Dobson
left her mark on the blaxploitation genre

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:32.140
with Cleopatra Jones, a kickass 1973 film
about a woman who works as supermodel as a

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.020
cover for her real job: spying for the U.S.
government.

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:39.350
It's a pretty fun premise and perfect for
a remake, and that's why Warner Bros. has

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:44.660
hired Misha Green, creator of the WGN show
Underground, to pen a script and create what

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.880
Deadline calls "the female answer to James
Bond."

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.140
Sounds promising!

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.060
West Side Story

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:56.040
While it might not begin tonight, production
on a brand new West Side Story will start

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.380
in the very near future.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.340
This remake of the 1961 classic will be directed
by Steven Spielberg, making his first musical.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:07.500
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Spielberg
has been wanting to direct this film "for

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:12.520
decades," and now he's teaming up with screenwriter
Tony Kushner to make his dream come true.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:17.340
Spielberg and Kushner previously worked together
on Lincoln and Munich, and as Kushner has

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:22.560
won an Emmy, a Tony, and the Pulitzer, we
can safely assume the script is in capable

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.060
hands.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:28.320
As for the cast, the filmmakers sent out a
casting call in January 2018, searching for

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:33.660
actors ages 15 to 25 to play the lead parts
of Tony, Maria, Anita, and Bernardo.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:38.360
And thankfully, unlike the original film,
Spielberg plans on casting the lead Latino

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:41.680
characters with actual Latino actors — which
is cool.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:43.640
48 Hrs.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:49.040
Hot off Saturday Night Live, Eddie Murphy
made his feature film debut with 48 Hrs.,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:53.520
which basically created the "buddy cop" genre
while becoming a box office smash.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:58.400
The action comedy is widely considered an
'80s classic, but now it's getting a 21st-century

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:58.900
spin.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:04.519
Jerrod Carmichael is set to star and co-write
the project, while brothers Josh and Ben Safdie,

00:11:04.519 --> 00:11:09.259
who previously directed the critically acclaimed
films Heaven Knows What and Good Time, will

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.460
be behind the cameras.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:11.740
Rabid

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:17.240
When it comes to body horror, it doesn't get
any better — or bloodier — than the work

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.540
of David Cronenberg.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:23.000
Though most of his films are famous, back
when he was still rising through the ranks,

00:11:23.019 --> 00:11:28.829
he directed the forgotten 1977 cult flick
Rabid, which presaged the whole "zombie plague"

00:11:28.829 --> 00:11:29.520
strain of films.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.300
And now it's going to be remade by Jen and
Sylvia Soska.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.379
Known to horror fans as the Twisted Twins,
the duo is set to begin filming the Rabid

00:11:38.379 --> 00:11:43.910
remake in April, 2018 with what Indiewire
calls a "modern and relevant spin from the

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.680
woman's perspective."

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.340
We sure can't wait!

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.020
Thanks for watching!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.580
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

